WEBVTT

00:00.240 --> 00:02.175
- [Voiceover] We're
asked, which value for D,

00:02.175 --> 00:03.924
and we see D in this equation here,

00:03.924 --> 00:08.677
makes X equals negative
three an extraneous solution

00:08.677 --> 00:10.377
for this radical equation?

00:10.377 --> 00:14.954
Squared of 3x plus 25
is equal to D plus 2x.

00:15.564 --> 00:17.609
And I encourage you to
pause the video and try to

00:17.609 --> 00:19.099
think about it on your own before we work

00:19.099 --> 00:20.499
through it together.

00:20.979 --> 00:23.930
Alright, now let's work
through this together.

00:23.930 --> 00:25.868
So the first thing that
just to remind ourselves

00:25.868 --> 00:27.720
is what is an extraneous solution?

00:27.720 --> 00:30.829
Well that's a solution that
we get or we think we get

00:30.829 --> 00:33.489
but it's really just a
by-product of how we solved it

00:33.489 --> 00:35.780
but isn't going to be an actual solution

00:35.780 --> 00:37.596
of our original equation.

00:37.596 --> 00:41.236
Now how do these extraneous
solutions pop up?

00:41.236 --> 00:44.759
Well, it pops up when you
take the square of both sides.

00:45.288 --> 00:47.333
So for this equation right
over here, to get rid

00:47.333 --> 00:49.919
of the radical, I'd want
to square both sides of it.

00:49.919 --> 00:52.731
If I square both sides, the
lefthand side will become

00:52.731 --> 00:57.345
3x plus 25 and the righthand
side, if I square this,

00:57.725 --> 00:59.113
is going to be, what?

00:59.113 --> 01:04.113
It's going to be D squared
plus 4, 4dx plus X squared.

01:06.501 --> 01:08.787
So that's just squaring
both sides of this,

01:08.887 --> 01:11.862
but notice, there's actually
a different equation than

01:11.862 --> 01:13.786
this one that if you squared
both sides, you would also

01:13.786 --> 01:14.772
get this.

01:14.772 --> 01:16.692
What is that different equation?

01:16.692 --> 01:18.753
Well the different equation
is if you took the negative

01:18.753 --> 01:20.549
of one of these sides.

01:20.549 --> 01:22.544
So for example, if you had,
if you started the original

01:22.544 --> 01:27.425
equation, the negative
square root of 3x plus 25

01:27.869 --> 01:32.035
plus 25, is equal to D plus 2x.

01:32.606 --> 01:35.508
You square both sides of this,
you still get this purple

01:35.668 --> 01:37.922
equation because you square a negative,

01:37.922 --> 01:39.765
you get a positive.

01:39.765 --> 01:42.471
So both of them, when
you square both sides,

01:42.471 --> 01:44.485
get us over here.

01:45.016 --> 01:47.021
And so when you solve
this purple equation,

01:47.021 --> 01:49.185
this is a quadratic right over here.

01:49.185 --> 01:50.252
You just rearrange it a little bit.

01:50.252 --> 01:52.103
You get into standard quadratic form,

01:52.103 --> 01:53.702
you'll get two solutions.

01:53.702 --> 01:55.259
And it turns out, one of
the solutions is going to be

01:55.259 --> 01:57.284
for this yellow equation
and one of the solutions

01:57.284 --> 01:58.788
is going to be for the purple equation.

01:59.344 --> 02:04.184
And if the solution that
is for the purple equation,

02:04.401 --> 02:06.425
is going to be an extraneous solution

02:06.511 --> 02:07.817
for the yellow equation.

02:07.817 --> 02:09.087
This is actually not
going to be a solution

02:09.087 --> 02:10.744
for the yellow equation.

02:10.821 --> 02:13.242
So when they say, "Which
value for D makes X equals

02:13.242 --> 02:15.314
"negative three and extraneous solution

02:15.314 --> 02:16.726
"for this yellow equation?"

02:17.070 --> 02:18.201
That's the same thing as saying,

02:18.201 --> 02:20.658
"What value of D makes
X equals negative three

02:20.658 --> 02:23.285
"a solution for this?"

02:24.105 --> 02:28.196
So a solution for this.

02:31.026 --> 02:32.990
If it's a solution for this,
it's going to be an extraneous

02:32.990 --> 02:35.442
solution for that 'cause these
are two different equations.

02:36.902 --> 02:38.255
We're taking the negative of just one side

02:38.255 --> 02:39.864
of this equation to get this one.

02:39.981 --> 02:41.588
If you took the negative
of both sides of this

02:41.588 --> 02:42.964
and that becomes the same
thing 'cause you could

02:42.964 --> 02:45.342
multiply both sides of an
equation times a negative value.

02:45.867 --> 02:49.128
So a solution for this, which
is equivalently a solution

02:49.128 --> 02:51.643
which is equivalent to a
solution, if I, instead of putting

02:51.643 --> 02:53.723
the negative on the lefthand
side, if I multiply the

02:53.723 --> 02:54.937
righthand side by the negative.

02:55.136 --> 02:57.711
But anyway, let's think
about which value for D

02:57.711 --> 03:02.232
makes X equals negative
three a solution for this?

03:03.111 --> 03:05.286
Well, let's substitute X
equals negative three here

03:05.286 --> 03:07.180
and then we just have to solve for D.

03:07.180 --> 03:09.468
If X equals negative three,
this is going to be negative

03:09.468 --> 03:12.791
the square root of three
times negative three

03:12.791 --> 03:17.287
is negative nine, plus 25 is equal to D.

03:18.445 --> 03:21.022
Two times negative three is negative six.

03:21.444 --> 03:26.444
So D minus 6, and so now we can

03:26.932 --> 03:31.387
square both sides of, we can square,

03:31.545 --> 03:32.485
actually let's do it this way.

03:32.485 --> 03:34.172
We can, I don't wanna
square both sides 'cause

03:34.172 --> 03:35.486
we lose some information.

03:35.486 --> 03:38.237
It's going to be the negative
square root of negative nine

03:38.237 --> 03:42.392
plus 25 is 16, is equal to D minus 6,

03:43.012 --> 03:46.983
so this is going to be
equal to negative four.

03:47.392 --> 03:48.549
Principle over 16 is four.

03:48.549 --> 03:49.982
We have the negative out front,

03:49.982 --> 03:54.029
is equal to D minus six and
then add six to both sides.

03:54.763 --> 03:58.894
You get two is equal
to, two is equal to D.

03:59.621 --> 04:01.816
So if D is equal to two here,

04:01.816 --> 04:05.179
if D is equal to two, then
a solution to this purple

04:05.179 --> 04:08.041
equation is going to be
X equals negative three.

04:08.689 --> 04:10.454
And so that would be an
extraneous solution because

04:10.624 --> 04:13.612
if X equals negative three
satisfies this over here,

04:13.612 --> 04:16.280
it's definitely gonna
satisfy this over here,

04:16.280 --> 04:19.240
but it's not going to
satisfy this up here.

04:19.401 --> 04:21.205
And you could verify this if this is equal

04:23.045 --> 04:25.856
to two, try out X equals negative three.

04:25.856 --> 04:27.848
You're gonna get on the lefthand side,

04:27.848 --> 04:30.816
you're going to get 16
and on the righthand side,

04:30.816 --> 04:34.625
you're gonna get two minus six which is

04:34.625 --> 04:36.355
equal to negative four.

04:37.574 --> 04:39.209
Two minus six which is negative four,

04:39.209 --> 04:40.520
so this does not work out.

04:40.520 --> 04:42.776
X equals negative three
is not a solution to this,

04:42.776 --> 04:45.639
but it is a solution for
this and it is a solution

04:45.639 --> 04:47.570
to this quadratic right over here.

04:47.730 --> 04:50.662
So D equals two makes
X equal negative three,

04:50.662 --> 04:54.172
an extraneous solution for this equation.
